  "methodology": "Other",
  "methodology_other": "Data were collected from Subnational Population Statistics from OCHA DR Congo, Enquete 123 Joint dataset (2005-2012) from the Democratic Republic of the Congo National Institute of Statistics, Humanitarian Tools, Registre de Mouvements from the UN International Organization for Migration, and the Humanitarian Response Plan from OCHA DR Congo. Census Bureau staff altered boundaries and modified the statistical data as detailed in the Metadata tab of the tabular data.",
  "name": "democratic-republic-of-the-congo-subnational-boundaries-and-tabular-data",
  "notes": "The geodatabase contains boundaries for the national and first- and second- order administrative divisions, aligned to the Large Scale International Boundaries dataset from the U.S. Department of State. The feature classes are suitable for linking to the attribute data provided. \r\n\r\nThe tabular data contain total population for 2019 (population estimates), household characteristics, IDP movements, people in need, and tribe and religion. ",
